1
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:05,250
(Sheldon:)I must say, Leonard...

2
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:10,610
(Sheldon:)...when I first heard your idea
for Giant Jenga I was skeptical.

3
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:16,610
(Leonard:)I can't blame you,
Tiny Twister was a complete bust.

4
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:18,000
Oh. But I was wrong.

5
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:22,760
(Sheldon:)The looming threat of being crushed
under a pile of lumber...

6
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:25,320
(Sheldon:)...does add a certain spice.

7
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:27,610
(Sheldon:)I've never felt so alive.

8
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:36,130
Oh, hello, Alex. Let me go get you
last night's recordings.

9
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:37,450
(Leonard:)What recordings?

10
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:39,960
(Sheldon:)Remember when you told me
I talk in my sleep?

11
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:44,280
(Sheldon:)It occurred to me that like most
things I say, it's probably pure gold.

12
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:47,280
(Sheldon:)So I started recording it all and...

13
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:49,130
(Sheldon:)...now Alex gets to comb through...

14
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:51,970
(Sheldon:)...eight hours of what I like to call
"Sheldon After Dark."

15
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:54,810
- Hey, Leonard.
- Hey.

16
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:56,770
(Leonard:)Just playing a little Giant Jenga.

17
00:00:56,920 --> 00:00:59,570
(Alex:)I know, I'm the one who
had to buy him the helmet.

18
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:02,450
So do you have plans this weekend?

19
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:06,320
(Leonard:)Most of Saturday's gonna be figuring out
where to put this game when we're done.

20
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:08,010
(Leonard:)How about you?

21
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:11,850
I'm gonna go hear Kip Thorne give a
lecture about subatomic space-time.

22
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,970
(Leonard:)Oh, that's his take on John Wheeler's
quantum foam. That should be great.

23
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:17,490
Well, you can come with me.

24
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:20,490
(Leonard:)I'd love to, but I'm supposed to
hang out with Penny.

25
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:24,000
- Well, bring her.
- Oh, she's not really into in that kind of stuff.

26
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:29,010
(Alex:)Well, if you want to hear about the lecture,
I can tell you all about it at work...

27
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:31,000
(Alex:)...or, you know, over dinner sometime.

28
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:32,370
(Leonard (jumping and knocking over the Jenga):)What?

29
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:40,020
Giant Jenga! I win!

